+## 28. Version 1.1: changes after the practice stop of 2026-10-07
+
+Version 1.0 was sealed and its practice set was built, in the folder `CASALESCENCE_NOETICS_v0_1`. The practice set stopped under the launch floor. The operator then wrote `PLAN_V1_1_CHANGE_SPEC.md` (2026-10-07). This section applies it. The v1.0 folder, the v1.0 plan and the v1.0 seal chain are not edited. They stay as evidence. Version 1.1 is built in a new study folder, `CASALESCENCE_NOETICS_v0_1__PLAN_v1_1`, a byte copy of the v1.0 folder (`PROJECT_COPY_RECORD.json`), from the question writer onward.
+
+### 28.1 Why: the counts
+
+All counts in this part are REAL. They were read from the sealed v1.0 practice evidence.
+
+- Practice set, 12 settings (all 4 reserve settings used): 48 role-step candidates after Steps 2 and 3; 30 after the key check (both solvers must pick the key with the passage); 16 after the no-passage check (both solvers right without the passage); 16 selected. Floor 36. Not met.
+- Plain-fact: 86 / 85 / 44 / 20 selected. Floor 20. Met.
+- Read-only diagnosis of the 18 key-check failures: 3 = the writer's key is wrong and a solver is right (all three BRING: TAKE_AWAY keyed the noticed thing, MEET_AGAIN keyed the remembered thing); 13 = the key is defensible but two or more options fit (7 of 11 PARTS candidates: WHAT_LEFT left two parts undone, NOT_BELONG had a second non-part among the wrong options; HABIT and LAND had near-synonym option sets); 1 = solver error on a sound question; 1 = the question omitted its own condition. Every one of the 11 solver flags sat on a question read as ambiguous or defective.
+- Of the 14 guessable items (dropped by the no-passage check): 5 = the key is the only option of its kind (an action among nouns, a memory among objects); 5 = valence written into the option words ("rough scratchy", "coarse", "heavy awkward", "calm"); 2 = the question repeats the answer's words; 2 = off-topic distractors (one leaked from another passage).
+- Supply: of 123 open (passage, form) pairs, 28 got no question from the writer, 42 lost every question at Steps 2 and 3, 53 had a passing question. The one-candidate-per-pair spare rule gave 48 candidates. Even 100% survival of 48 candidates could not have reached 36 after the per-passage cap. So v1.1 must raise supply AND question quality.
+
+### 28.2 Two loosened key rules, counted and rejected
+
+| Rule that was counted | REAL effect on the v1.0 practice set | Decision |
+|---|---|---|
+| Keep when one solver picks the key and the other flags | would add 3 tasks, all flawed | REJECTED |
+| Keep when the writer plus one solver agree | would add 6 tasks, four flawed and one with a wrong key | REJECTED |
+
+The key check and the no-passage check stay exactly as in v1.0.
